// FreeMount build defaults: project Google OAuth Desktop client + team.
//
// This ships a DEFAULT Google Desktop OAuth client on purpose. Desktop-app
// client credentials are public by design (they are embedded in every
// distributed desktop binary); they are NOT user secrets — user tokens and
// passwords live only in the macOS Keychain.
//
// Google may show an "unverified app" consent warning when signing in with
// Drive/GCS using this shared client, or you can create your own Desktop
// client in Google Cloud Console and replace the two values below.
// SFTP, WebDAV, SMB and FTP/FTPS need no OAuth client at all.
//
// Steps:
// 1. Copy this file to "Configs/Secrets.xcconfig" (or run
//    scripts/install-from-source.sh, which does everything).
// 2. Set DEVELOPMENT_TEAM to your own Apple ID team (the installer can
//    auto-detect it). Secrets.xcconfig stays git-ignored.

FREEMOUNT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID = 319728381325-v71u1mjithqc6ovqvbb4mnc0hhbf0r65.apps.googleusercontent.com
FREEMOUNT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET = 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

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = 
